<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Denkyira</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Denkyira was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> state in what is now southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> that dominated the region in the seventeenth century, holding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> as tributaries. Its defeat by the Asante under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osei-tutu-i">Osei Tutu</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-feyiase">Battle of Feyiase</a> in 1701 marked the emergence of the Ashanti Empire as the leading power of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/denkyira.jpg" alt="Denkyira" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denkyrian_Empire_1700ce.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
